---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Every crit runs on a provocation, an activity, and a discussion with no
    scripted answer. Bring what each one's brief below asks for; nothing else
    is assumed. All of them open with the same ten minutes of guided attention
    the lectures do.
  </p>
  <p>
    Several involve saying something out loud about your own thinking. In all
    of them you can pass, at any point, without giving a reason — nothing you
    share is marked, and nobody follows up.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The second half is partly yours to set.</strong> After
    <a href={withBase("/assessments/the-anonymous-thread/")}>the anonymous thread</a>, every
    technique students reported gets collected, stripped of identifying detail,
    and put to a vote on the forum. From the following week we try the
    room&rsquo;s picks one at a time — so the back half of this list grows out
    of what the cohort actually found useful, not out of what the teaching
    staff guessed.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no class in the mid-semester break, between weeks 6 and 7. The
    forum post is due then, and it is the only thing due that week.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
